  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Tensions rose between Stevens and El-Sayed over an ad run by an outside PAC, and on November 1, 2026, Stevens appeared with Republican nominee Mike Rogers at The Perfecting Church in Detroit.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383807510:53"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "Stevens followed her fiancé in endorsing Rogers on November 1, which led to a rift between her and El-Sayed.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383807510:97"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Haley Maria Stevens, born June 24, 1983, is an American politician who has served as a U.S. representative since 2019.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383807510:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Haley Stevens was born on 24 June 1983 in Rochester Hills.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q58322563:P569",
        "wd:Q58322563:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "She was educated at Seaholm High School and American University.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q58322563:P69:Q7440488",
        "wd:Q58322563:P69:Q168000"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:37Z",
      "text": "She has worked in Washington, D.C.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q58322563:P937:Q61"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:43Z",
      "text": "Readers also turned to pages on Abdul El-Sayed (243,340), Mike Rogers (Michigan politician) (77,353), and the 2026 United States Senate election in Michigan (60,512).",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Abdul_El-Sayed:2026-11-02",
        "views:en:Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician):2026-11-02",
        "views:en:2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan:2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:52Z",
      "text": "On 2 November 2026, 548,345 people read about Haley Stevens, about 519 times the usual daily level.",
      "cites": [
